# Line endings, pinned to LF on every platform, because this repo is now
# developed on both macOS and Windows and the tooling assumes LF.
#
# The failure this exists to prevent: tools/test_app.mjs loads the app's
# classic scripts by concatenating them and stripping strict mode with
# `src.replace(/"use strict";\n/g, "")` before an indirect eval. That regex
# does not match ";\r\n". On a Windows checkout under git's default
# core.autocrlf=true, strict mode therefore survived the strip, core.js's
# implicit globals became assignments to undeclared names, and the whole suite
# died on its first line with "ReferenceError: DB is not defined". Several
# other regexes in tools/ are anchored the same way.
#
# Normalising the working tree is the cheap fix; making every such regex
# CRLF-tolerant is the expensive one. macOS is unaffected either way — it
# already checked out LF, and the blobs in the index are unchanged.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: no eol translation, no attempt to diff them as text.
*.png   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.stl   binary
